                        <field name="dc_description">The railway Angermünde - Stralsund was one of the Prussian state railways. Since the 1860s, consideration has been given to the continuation of the railway to Sweden on the island of Rügen. The connection between Stralsund and the island by means of two railway ferries was established in 1882/3. The Prussian state railways have built and operated such ferries and laying points on their own. The elaborate model was built at the end of the 19th century and restored in 1987.<br/>
<br/>
Traffic and construction museum. Official guide through the collections/Transport and Construction Museum Berlin. Berlin: Elsner, 1943. p.155 (Deutsches Technikmuseum) </field>
